{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Payment Plans",
    "description": "A set of endpoints to manage payment plans in the sales domain. A payment plan collects a fixed amount from a client's saved card on a recurring schedule. A plan is either **standalone**, where every installment is an independent charge, or **linked** to an existing payment request through `payment_request_uid`, where every installment is collected against an open invoice and reduces its balance until it is fully paid.\n\nThese endpoints supersede the legacy `/business/payments/v1/scheduled_payments_rules` API. The legacy endpoints remain available and unchanged, but they do not support linking a plan to a payment request.\n\n## Differences from the legacy v1 API\nThe response shape is otherwise identical to `/business/payments/v1/scheduled_payments_rules` — the v3 endpoints delegate to the same components, so no field that v1 returns today stops being returned. Two fields are added:\n\n* **`payment_request_uid`** - links the plan to a payment request. Null for a standalone plan.\n* **`cancel_reason`** - identifies a plan that the system closed because its linked payment request is no longer collectable.\n\n**`amount` and `amount_paid` are JSON numbers.** The legacy v1 endpoints return them as quoted strings (`\"10.0\"`); v3 returns `10.0`, matching every other v3 money field (`invoice.grand_total`, `creditNote.total_amount`, `estimate.amount`).\n\nOne field is dropped: **`rrule` is not returned.** v1 exposes the plan's schedule as a serialized IceCube YAML document — an internal representation whose format is a library detail, not a contract. `start_date`, `frequency_type`, `cycles`, `end_date` and `next_payment_time` describe the schedule completely.",
    "version": "1.0",
    "contact": {}
  },
  "tags": [],
