      "post": {
        "operationId": "createPaymentPlan",
        "summary": "Create a PaymentPlan",
        "description": "## Overview\nCreate a PaymentPlan that charges the client's saved card on a recurring schedule.\n\nOmit `payment_request_uid` to create a **standalone** plan, where every installment is an independent charge. Supply it to create a **linked** plan, where every installment is collected against that payment request's open invoice and reduces its balance.\n\n## Calculating `amount` for a linked plan\nThe server validates `amount` rather than deriving it, so the caller sends the per-installment amount it wants. Divide the invoice's open balance by `cycles` and **round up** to two decimals — `ceil(balance / cycles, 2)`. Rounding up is deliberate: the plan's nominal total then slightly exceeds the balance, and the final installment is automatically clamped down to whatever is actually left, so the invoice lands on exactly zero. Rounding down would leave a residue that no installment ever collects.\n\nFor a 1,000.00 invoice over 3 cycles, send `amount: 333.34`. The plan collects 333.34, 333.34 and then 333.32.\n\n## Conditionally required fields\n`cycles` is required for every `frequency_type` except `one_time`. For a `one_time` plan it is ignored and stored as 1.\n\n## Prerequisites\n1. The business has the `scheduled_payments` feature enabled.\n2. The business has a payment gateway configured that supports recurring payments. PayPal is not supported.\n3. The card in `payment_method.uid` is active, belongs to the matter's client, and uses the same payment provider as the business's payment gateway.\n4. For a linked plan, the business has the `rollout.payments.payment_plans` feature flag enabled.\n\n## Eligibility of a linked payment request\nThe payment request must belong to the caller's business, sit on the same matter as the plan, be an **open invoice** (not draft, cancelled or archived, with no payment already pending), carry the same currency, have a positive balance, and have no other active plan linked to it. The plan must also not overshoot the balance before its final payment — `amount x (cycles - 1)` must be **less than** the open balance. Each failure returns a validation error on `payment_request_uid`.\n\nFind eligible payment requests with `GET /business/payments/v1/payment_requests?filter[matter_uid][eq]={matter_uid}&filter[entity_type][in]=Invoice&filter[state][in]=DUE,OVERDUE`.\n\nAvailable for **Staff Tokens**.",
        "parameters": [],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "name": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/name"
                  },
                  "description": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/description"
                  },
                  "payment_request_uid": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/payment_request_uid"
                  },
                  "amount": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/amount"
                  },
                  "currency": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/currency"
                  },
                  "cycles": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/cycles"
                  },
                  "frequency_type": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/frequency_type"
                  },
                  "start_date": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/start_date"
                  },
                  "matter_uid": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/matter_uid"
                  },
                  "send_receipt": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/send_receipt"
                  },
                  "payment_method": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/payment_method"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "name",
                  "amount",
                  "currency",
                  "frequency_type",
                  "start_date",
                  "matter_uid",
                  "send_receipt",
                  "payment_method"
                ]
              },
              "example": {
                "name": "Kitchen remodel plan",
                "description": "3 monthly installments for invoice #1042",
                "payment_request_uid": "a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8",
                "amount": 333.34,
                "currency": "USD",
                "cycles": 3,
                "frequency_type": "monthly",
                "start_date": "2026-09-01T09:00:00Z",
                "matter_uid": "m1m2m3m4m5m6m7m8",
                "send_receipt": true,
                "payment_method": {
                  "type": "card",
                  "uid": "c1c2c3c4c5c6c7c8"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "The PaymentPlan was created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "allOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/response.json"
                    },
                    {
                      "properties": {
