      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updatePaymentPlan",
        "summary": "Update a PaymentPlan",
        "description": "## Overview\nUpdate a PaymentPlan. Only two changes are possible, and they are the only fields this endpoint accepts:\n\n* **Change the card** — send `payment_method`. The new card must be active, belong to the matter's client, and use the same payment provider as the business's payment gateway. It is charged from the next installment onwards.\n* **Cancel the plan** — send `status: \"cancelled\"`. No further installment is collected and the schedule is deactivated. Installments already collected are **not** refunded; for a linked plan, whatever was already paid stays applied to the invoice, and the invoice becomes editable again immediately.\n\n## Why cancelling is an update\nv3 forbids action suffixes on a resource path, so the legacy `PUT /business/payments/v1/scheduled_payments_rules/{uid}/cancel` becomes a state change on the resource itself. `cancelled` is the only status a client may set. `completed` is owned by the system, and cancelling a plan that is no longer `active` is rejected.\n\n## What cannot be changed\n`payment_request_uid` is immutable — a plan cannot be relinked to a different payable, and a standalone plan cannot become linked. `amount`, `currency`, `cycles`, `frequency_type` and `start_date` are fixed at creation; cancel the plan and create a new one instead.\n\nAvailable for **Staff Tokens**.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "uid",
            "required": true,
            "in": "path",
            "description": "Unique identifier of the PaymentPlan",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "example": "7gilictbt12jir3v"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "At least one of `payment_method` or `status` must be supplied.",
                "properties": {
                  "payment_method": {
                    "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/sales/paymentPlan.json#/properties/payment_method"
                  },
                  "status": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Set to `cancelled` to stop the plan. This is the only value a client may set (e.g., \"cancelled\")",
                    "enum": [
                      "cancelled"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "minProperties": 1
              },
              "example": {
                "status": "cancelled"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The updated PaymentPlan",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "allOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "https://vcita.github.io/developers-hub/entities/response.json"
                    },
                    {
                      "properties": {
